<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Johnnic half yr shr up 15.2 pct, div rises.</title>
<headline>Johnnic half yr shr up 15.2 pct, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr: (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline	   114	 vs   99</p>
<p>    - equity acctd     261	 vs   99</p>
<p>    Div (cts)	     21	 vs   18</p>
<p>    Attrib income	269.8     vs   31.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income	269.8     vs   31.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		284.3     vs   34.4</p>
<p>    Tax		     13.3     vs    1.8</p>
<p>    Turnover	     180.9     vs   86.2</p>
<p>    Share of assoc     127.5     vs  115.7</p>
<p>Div payable: April 16</p>
<p>On register: March 15</p>
<p>Full name: Johnnies Industrial Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that despite the slowdown in residential property sales and the general weakness in the South African consumer market, it expected headline earnings for the year to reflect growth similar to that achieved in the first six months.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
